{#
  Sourced from the developer's shell rc file. Written 0600 because it can hold
  the OTLP bearer; the rc file itself only ever gains a `.` line, so a
  committed dotfiles repo leaks nothing.

  `sh_quote` is not decoration: values include identity attributes taken from
  the access token, so an apostrophe in a display name would otherwise close
  the quote and leave the shell parsing the rest as code.
-#}
# Written by `governance-auth`. Mode 0600 on purpose: this file can hold a
# credential. It is sourced from your shell rc file so the rc file itself
# stays safe to commit.
{% for name, value in exports -%}
export {{ name }}={{ value | sh_quote }}
{% endfor -%}
